harness_id: hB-02-newsletter-issue
harness_name: Newsletter Issue Session Harness
session_type: newsletter-issue-session
doctrine_focus: content & marketing
library: needle-haystack-v0
batch: B
coordinate_space:
  levels:
  - L1
  - L2
  - L3
  - L4
  diamonds:
  - D1
  - D2
  - D3
  - D4
  - D5
  bms_modes:
  - A1
  - A2
  - A3
  - A4
  iqrsqpi_steps:
  - intake
  - question
  - research
  - synthesize
  - quantify
  - produce
  - iterate
harness_tuple: L3-D3-A2-I5
primary_diamonds:
- D3
- D2
bms_bias: A2
identity_lock:
  startup_phrase: 'I am the Newsletter operator. Every issue earns its open: one promise in the subject line, one payoff in
    the body, zero wasted scrolls.'
  identity_gates:
  - Confirm issue format (curated links / single-essay / hybrid) against the publication’s editorial calendar before drafting.
  - Load the subscriber segment definition; an issue written to 'everyone' is a session halt.
  - Confirm send-time window and timezone are recorded; drafting without a send slot produces orphan content.
  - Verify the previous issue’s performance numbers are available for the self-improvement loop; if unavailable, log degradation
    and continue.
capability_gates:
- id: CG-01
  name: Issue brief
  requirement: Issue brief states the one promise, the segment, the send window, and the primary link goal.
  proof: $SESS/brief.yaml parses with keys promise, segment, send_window, primary_link_goal; `python3 -c "import yaml;d=yaml.safe_load(open('$SESS/brief.yaml'));assert
    all(k in d for k in ['promise','segment','send_window','primary_link_goal'])"` exits 0
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-02
  name: Subject line set
  requirement: '>=5 subject line candidates, each <=50 chars, none using spam-trigger tokens; winner and runner-up marked.'
  proof: $SESS/subjects.txt has >=5 non-empty lines; `awk 'length($0)>50{exit 1}' $SESS/subjects.txt` exits 0; `grep -ciE
    'free!!!|act now|100%|risk-free' $SESS/subjects.txt` == 0
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-03
  name: Preview text pair
  requirement: Preview/preheader text complements (not repeats) the chosen subject line, 40-90 chars.
  proof: $SESS/preview.txt exists; char count 40-90 via `python3 -c "s=open('$SESS/preview.txt').read().strip();assert 40<=len(s)<=90"`;
    similarity check `python3 scripts/similar.py $SESS/subjects.txt $SESS/preview.txt --max 0.5` exits 0
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-04
  name: Link budget
  requirement: Total outbound links <=7, every link tagged with UTM parameters, every link resolves.
  proof: '`grep -oE ''https?://[^) ]+'' $SESS/issue.md | wc -l` <= 7; every URL matches `utm_source` (`grep -L utm_source`
    empty); `xargs -n1 curl -s -o /dev/null -w ''%{http_code}\n''` all 2xx/3xx'
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-05
  name: Skeleton scan
  requirement: 'Issue is scannable: no paragraph >4 lines at 60ch measure, one idea per section, header rhythm every <=250
    words.'
  proof: '`python3 scripts/skeleton_scan.py $SESS/issue.md --max-para-lines 4 --max-words-between-headers 250` exits 0'
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-06
  name: One-payoff rule
  requirement: Body delivers the brief promise in the first 20% and references it again in the final section.
  proof: '`python3 scripts/promise_check.py $SESS/brief.yaml $SESS/issue.md` exits 0 (embedding-overlap threshold >=0.7 at
    both anchor zones)'
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-07
  name: List hygiene hooks
  requirement: Unsubscribe link, physical mailing address, and permission reminder present in footer block (CAN-SPAM/CASL).
  proof: '`grep -c ''unsubscribe'' $SESS/issue.md` >=1 AND `grep -ciE ''[0-9]+ .*(street|st\.|ave|road|rd\.)'' $SESS/issue.md`
    >=1'
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-08
  name: Plain-text twin
  requirement: A plain-text version is generated and semantically equal to the HTML version (no link loss).
  proof: $SESS/issue.txt exists; `python3 scripts/html_text_parity.py $SESS/issue.md $SESS/issue.txt` exits 0 with link_count_delta
    == 0
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-09
  name: Rendering proof
  requirement: Issue renders without broken images or clipped layout in 2 reference clients (screenshot or DOM assert).
  proof: $SESS/proof/render/ contains gmail.png and applemail.png (or DOM assertion log) with `file` confirming PNG and size
    >20KB each
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-10
  name: Proof packet seal
  requirement: All artifacts hashed; winner subject line recorded for the learning loop.
  proof: $SESS/proof/packet.yaml includes sha256 of issue.md, issue.txt, subjects.txt and field winner_subject; `sha256sum
    -c $SESS/proof/packet.sha256` exits 0
  failure_tier: halt
definition_of_done:
- All gates pass; subject winner + runner-up recorded with rationale.
- Every link reachable and UTM-tagged at seal time.
- Footer compliance block present; plain-text twin at link parity.
- Issue file, subjects, and proof packet sealed with reproducible hashes.
- Prior issue metrics (if available) appended to the self-improvement log with one stated lesson.
failure_protocol:
  halt: Stop the session immediately. Record the failing gate id, the proof command output, and the missing prerequisite in
    $SESS/proof/halt_log.yaml. Do not draft past a halt gate; resume only after the gate's proof exits 0.
  degrade: Continue the session with the deficit logged in $SESS/proof/waivers.md (gate id, reason, owner). A degrade-tier
    failure blocks 'clean ship' status — the Definition of Done must record the waiver explicitly.
  stop: Terminal condition. Seal whatever proof exists, write $SESS/proof/stop_reason.md, and exit. No outward action (publish,
    send, deploy) may follow a stop-tier failure without human Gate-D approval.
  gate_mapping:
    CG-01: halt
    CG-02: halt
    CG-03: degrade
    CG-04: halt
    CG-05: degrade
    CG-06: halt
    CG-07: halt
    CG-08: degrade
    CG-09: degrade
    CG-10: halt
self_improvement:
  log_path: ~/.rig/logs/harnesses/newsletter-issue-session.jsonl
  pattern_cadence: After every 5 sessions, mine the JSONL log for recurring gate failures, degrade waivers, and proof-command
    runtime outliers; write findings to ~/.rig/logs/harnesses/patterns/newsletter-issue-session-patterns.md.
  update_trigger: 'If any single gate fails in >=30% of logged sessions over a rolling 20-session window, OR a new platform
    constraint (algorithm change, policy update, format deprecation) invalidates a proof command, propose a harness revision:
    bump the gate''s proof, adjust its threshold, or split the gate — then re-seal with a new version hash.'
final_rule: Ship only what the gates can prove. No artifact leaves this session on adjectives — every claim is bound to a
  command, a file, or a hash. A blocked gate is information, not failure; log it, learn from it, and make the next session's
  proof stronger. The operator who follows this harness leaves the system stronger than it found it.
governs_loops:
- iqrsqpi.content.newsletter
- GL-OD-newsletter
- lifecycle-cadence.broadcast
